This is a copy of github.com/masahiro331/go-ext4-filesystem at
v0.0.0-20261121070946-2c847b6f8831 (Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE),
used by BackupZit through a replace directive in its go.mod.

Upstream now has the fixes this copy carried before (extents of the full
length 32768 read as zeros, upstream #24 from BackupZit PR #49 by gtawelt;
symbolic links followed at most 40 times and relative targets resolved in
the link's folder). Changes by BackupZit that upstream does not have
(2026-11-20, rebased onto this version 2026-11-23):
- ext4/fs.go: NewFS refuses an implausible superblock (block size above
  64 KiB, inode size below 128 bytes or above the block size, more groups
  than the volume holds); upstream checks only for zero blocks or inodes
  per group.
- ext4/ext4.go: the extent tree walk stops after as many nodes and extents
  as the volume has blocks (at most 4 Mi): a crafted tree can point many
  internal nodes at one block.
- The upstream tests are left out.

Drop this copy once upstream has these checks.
